// Wuxia: original stories written for this game. Format: docs/v3/BLUEPRINT-FORMAT.md.

== wuxia.f01 | feature | journey
title: The Escort Of One Coffin
genre: wuxia + adventure
tone: Dusty, laconic and honour-bound
era: 1640 | period
setting: The post road from the northern frontier to the Yangtze, in the last years of a dynasty | fictional | road
logline: The last guard of a bankrupt armed-escort house accepts one final contract, to carry a disgraced general's coffin a thousand miles home, and finds that every faction in a collapsing empire wants what is, or is not, inside it.
premise: Escort houses carry silver and people along roads the state can no longer keep. They live by a flag, a shouted name and an understanding with the bandits. The house {lin_yue} was raised in has lost its master, its men and its credit. She has the flag and the cart. A widow pays in advance for one coffin, north to south, to be buried among ancestors.
synopsis: The journey gives the film its shape: a road, a load, and a rule that an escort never opens the cargo. {lin_yue} travels with a mule, an old cook, {uncle_ba}, who was once the house's best spear, and the client's servant, a scholarly boy, {little_seal}. At the first river crossing, bandits who should honour the flag do not; their chief has been paid. At an inn, a court eunuch's swordsman, {the_crane}, elegant and bored, offers ten times the fee for an hour alone with the coffin. In the mountains, a rebel captain wants it for his own reasons. Each believes something different: that the general is not dead; that the coffin holds the frontier army's pay; that it holds the seal that commands the northern garrisons; that it holds evidence against the eunuch. {lin_yue} does not want to know. The house's whole meaning was that it delivered. The second act tests that. {uncle_ba} is killed holding a bridge with a kitchen cleaver and a carrying pole, in the film's great set piece. {little_seal} confesses he is the general's son. {the_crane}, who fights her twice and does not kill her either time, says what the film has been asking: a code is a fine thing in a world that keeps its side of it; whom does she think she is being honest for? In the third act she reaches the river with soldiers of three factions converging. She has earned the right, and has the need, and opens the coffin. Inside is the general, dead, in a plain robe, with no seal and no silver: only a list in his own hand of the frontier soldiers owed pay, and the amounts. It was what he was disgraced for asking for. {the_crane} reads it and, for the first time, has nothing clever to say; he lets the cart pass and turns to face the others on the road. She buries the general where the widow asked. She nails the list to the door of the prefecture. She folds the flag and keeps it.
question: What is a promise worth when the world it was made in is ending?
themes: keeping faith as its own purpose; the load nobody understands; the debts of states
audience: Adults and teenagers; martial-arts fans who like their heroes tired and honourable
viewpoint: With {lin_yue}; the coffin's contents are withheld from the audience as from her
stakes: Her life and her companions', the house's name, and whatever is in the box
conflict: One escort and her code against three factions, a thousand miles and her own curiosity
ending: She delivers. The coffin held only a dead man and a list of what soldiers were owed. She posts the list and keeps the flag.
experience: Clean, wide-open action, a bridge you will not forget, and a reveal that lands as sorrow, not a twist
look: Yellow dust, a black lacquer coffin on a cart, an escort flag; fights filmed wide in real places
sound: Cart axle, mule bells, the escort's road cry. A cleaver on a spear shaft. Wind.
m: keep | system | loyalty-vs-truth | bittersweet
@ lin_yue | Lin Yue | lead | protagonist | human | she/her | 31 | To deliver the load and close the house honourably | The flag is all her master left | Everyone wants the cargo and she has sworn not to look | Laconic, stubborn, dryly funny | From the last employee of a dead firm to the keeper of its meaning | Short sentences; the road cry | Dusty riding clothes, a straight sword, a rolled flag
@ uncle_ba | Uncle Ba | supporting | mentor | human | he/him | 64 | One more road, and a good dinner at the end | He cannot imagine not going | He is old and they are many | Garrulous, sly, brave without fuss | From cook to the house's best spear one last time | Grumbles, recipes, old stories | Apron, a cleaver, a carrying pole
@ little_seal | Little Seal | supporting | ally | human | he/him | 16 | His father buried at home | He promised his mother | He has lied about who he is | Bookish, earnest, steadier than he looks | From servant to acknowledged son | Formal, classical quotations | Scholar's cap too big, ink-stone in his bundle
@ the_crane | The Crane | co-lead | rival | human | he/him | 36 | To be given a reason | He serves a master he despises, superbly | He has met someone who keeps her word | Elegant, bored, lethal, curious | From hired sword to a man who turns round on the road | Courteous irony | White robe, a slender sword, a fan
~ lin_yue - uncle_ba | escort and old hand | he calls her "young master" as a joke | she shouts the house's name for him at the bridge
~ lin_yue - the_crane | escort and court swordsman | an offer of ten times the fee | he guards her back, unasked
~ lin_yue - little_seal | escort and client's servant | a boy to be kept out of the way | a son she delivers along with his father
# The Contract | INT | Escort House, Empty Hall | DAY | lin_yue, uncle_ba, little_seal | Take the load | Dust sheets, unpaid bills, one flag. A widow's silver. A lacquer coffin. The rule: we do not open the cargo | The last contract | 5 | props=coffin+escort flag
# The Road | EXT | River Ford | DAY | lin_yue, uncle_ba, little_seal | Find the flag ignored | She gives the road cry. The bandits should stand aside. They do not. A fight in the shallows, quick and ugly | The code no longer holds | 6 | water, crowd=20, stunts=river fight, animals=mule
# The Road | INT | Roadside Inn | NIGHT | lin_yue, the_crane | Be offered ten times | A man in white, a fan, perfect manners. An hour alone with the coffin. She says the house does not sell hours. They fight between tables; he stops first | {the_crane} lets her live | 7 | crowd=30, stunts=inn duel with wire work
# The Bridge | EXT | Mountain Rope Bridge | DAY | lin_yue, uncle_ba, little_seal | Hold it | Rebels behind. The cart must cross. {uncle_ba} stays on the planks with a cleaver and a pole. She shouts the house's name for him from the far side | {uncle_ba} dies holding the bridge | 8 | crowd=40, stunts=bridge battle with heavy wire work, vfx=gorge
# The Bridge | EXT | Hillside Camp | NIGHT | lin_yue, little_seal | Hear a confession | The boy says whose son he is. She says it changes nothing about the delivery. She does not sleep | | 4 | props=campfire
# The River | EXT | Post Road, Above The Yangtze | DAY | lin_yue, the_crane | Be asked why | Second duel, in the open. He disarms her and gives the sword back. Whom is she being honest for? She says: the house | | 6 | stunts=open-road duel with wire work
# The River | EXT | River Landing | DUSK | lin_yue, the_crane, little_seal | Open it | Three banners closing in. She opens the lid. A dead man in a plain robe, and a list of soldiers and sums. {the_crane} reads it and turns to face the road | The coffin is opened | 7 | water, crowd=150, stunts=standoff, props=coffin+pay list
# The River | EXT | Prefecture Gate | DAWN | lin_yue, little_seal | Deliver | A grave among ancestors. A list nailed to an official door. A flag folded, and kept | | 4 | props=escort flag+pay list
